/*  Axioms — source in another language held by a Cufet name: `TypeChecker.Foreign.cs`.

    ★ The parser lowers a `regex` pattern, and a `cufet` block that says what it gives back, into
    an ordinary `Bind` marked `:FromAxiomLanguage`. All a lowered function still owes is the pull
    its language wants around it, since the literal that would have asked is gone.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The value of a mark a parsed node carries after its fields — `:FromAxiomLanguage "regex"` — or "".
    /// A mark is an atom starting with `:`, which no field's leaf can be.
    Bind text to bind-mark, given (the node statement, the text mark):
        Define place as 1.
        While place is less than the number of statement's children, repeat:
            Define here as cast field-of on (statement, place).
            If here's kind is "atom" and here's word is mark:
                // A text is quoted; a fact like `true` is not.
                Define held as cast field-of on (statement, place + 1).
                If held's word starts with "\"", return cast unquoted on (held).
                Return held's word.
            Done.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind fact to has-mark, given (the node statement, the text mark):
        For each here in statement's children, repeat:
            If here's kind is "atom" and here's word is mark, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// A language book's name as it is spoken — `the c-language`, plain `regex`.
    Bind text to language-named, given (the text language):
        If (language in lowercase) is "c-language", return "the {language}".
        Return language.
    Done.

    /// `RequireLanguagePulled`: the book of this language, or its Cufet layer, is in scope.
    Bind void or failure to require-language-pulled unto checker, given (the text language, the number at-row):
        Define wanted as language in lowercase.
        For each scope in one's scopes, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as (the value of pair)'s shape.
                If held's kind is "BookType" or held's kind is "ObjectType":
                    If (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 1)) in lowercase) is wanted, return.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the {language} book is not in scope", "",
            at-row, "write {language} source without pulling the {language} book",
            "Add 'Pull a book on {cast language-named on (language)}.' around this.")).
    Done.

    // ── C axioms: `Define c-language number answer as [6 * 7].` ───────────

    /// A book that names a language rather than a library.
    Bind fact to is-language-book, given (the text name):
        Define lowered as name in lowercase.
        Return lowered is "c-language" or lowered is "cufet" or lowered is "regex".
    Done.

    Bind text to amount-of, given (the number amount, the text noun):
        If amount is 1, return "1 {noun}".
        Return "{amount} {noun}s".
    Done.

    /// The `(type name)` pairs an axiom literal says it takes.
    Bind series of node to axiom-parameters, given (the node literal):
        Define found as a series of node.
        Define place as 4.
        While place is less than the number of literal's children, repeat:
            If (cast field-of on (literal, place))'s word is ":Parameters":
                For each pair in (cast field-of on (literal, place + 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Insert pair into found.
                Done.
            Done.
            Increment place by 2.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// Where an axiom literal stands — the key its tag is kept under.
    Bind text to literal-key, given (the node literal):
        Return "{(cast field-of on (literal, 2))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (literal, 3))'s word}".
    Done.

    /// `ForeignC.Mentions`: `the <name>` in the source — the article in any case, the name exact,
    /// and a dash counting as part of a name on either side.
    Bind fact to mentions-parameter, given (the text source, the text name):
        Define lowered as source in lowercase.
        Define total as the length of source.
        Define spot as 1.
        While spot + 2 is not greater than total, repeat:
            If the characters from spot to spot + 2 of lowered is "the" and cast name-edge on (source, spot - 1):
                Define past-article as spot + 3.
                Define spaced as past-article.
                While spaced is not greater than total and cast is-blank-char on (the characters from spaced to spaced of source), repeat:
                    Increment spaced by 1.
                Done.
                Define ending as spaced + the length of name - 1.
                If spaced is greater than past-article and ending is not greater than total:
                    If the characters from spaced to ending of source is name and cast name-edge on (source, ending + 1), return true.
                Done.
            Done.
            Increment spot by 1.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Nothing of a name at this place — the start or end of the text, or a character no name holds.
    Bind fact to name-edge, given (the text source, the number spot):
        If spot is less than 1 or spot is greater than the length of source, return true.
        Define here as the characters from spot to spot of source.
        Return cast name-character on (here) is false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to name-character, given (the text letter):
        If letter is "-" or letter is "_", return true.
        Return "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789" contains letter.
    Done.

    /// ⚠ C#'s `\s` also takes a form feed and a vertical tab, and neither can be written in Cufet —
    /// there is no escape for them and no way to make a character from its code (ROADMAP › Measured
    /// needs, character classification). Between `the` and a name in C source, they do not occur.
    Bind fact to is-blank-char, given (the text letter):
        Return letter is " " or letter is "\t" or letter is "\n" or letter is "\r".
    Done.

    /// `TagAxiomDeclaration`: a `Define` whose value is foreign source gets its language from the
    /// declaration, and the declared type is completed from what the literal takes.
    Bind node or failure to tag-axiom-declaration unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define define-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Define declared as cast field-of on (statement, 7).
        If declared's kind is "ObjectType" and cast is-filled-type on (declared) is false:
            Define shell-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declared, 1)).
            If cast is-language-book on (shell-name):
                The declared becomes cast made on ("AxiomType", a series with (cast quoted on (shell-name), cast nothing, cast listed)).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If value's kind is not "AxiomLiteral":
            If cast bind-mark on (statement, ":HasParameterClause") is "true":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is not foreign source, so it cannot be 'given' anything",
                    "Only an axiom — source in another language — takes parameters at a 'Define'",
                    define-row, "declare parameters for '{name}'",
                    "Use 'Bind ... to {name}, given (...)' for a function, or drop the clause.")).
            Done.
            Return declared.
        Done.
        Define literal-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (value, 2)).
        If declared's kind is not "AxiomType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is foreign source, but nothing says what language it is in",
                "Square brackets say the text is not Cufet; they cannot say which language it is, and the tag names who reads it",
                literal-row, "write foreign source without naming its language",
                "Name it in the declaration: 'Define c-language {name} as [ ... ].'")).
        Done.
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declared, 1)).
        Define released as cast literal-mark on (value, ":ReleasedBy").
        If (language in lowercase) is "cufet" and released is not "":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is Cufet source, so there is nothing for it to free",
                "A release clause hands memory back to the language that allocated it, and cufet source allocates nothing across a boundary — what it produces is an ordinary Cufet value",
                literal-row, "give '{name}' a release clause", "Drop the ', and free it with ...' clause.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's require-language-pulled on (language, literal-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define result as cast field-of on (declared, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (result) is false, the result becomes cast one's resolved on (result).
        // Written onto the literal, so everything that runs it carries them along — C#'s
        // AxiomLiteral.Language and ReturnType.
        Cast note on (value, ":Language", cast quoted on (language)).
        Cast note on (value, ":ReturnType", result).
        If cast is-nothing on (result) is false:
            Cast require-crossable-result on (result, language, literal-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define parameters as cast axiom-parameters on (value).
        Cast one's check-axiom-parameters on (statement, value, language, result, parameters) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-release-clause on (value, released, language, result, literal-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define parameter-types as cast listed.
        For each pair in parameters, repeat:
            Cast parameter-types's add on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
        Done.
        Define tagged as cast made on ("AxiomType", a series with (cast quoted on (language), result, parameter-types)).
        In one's axiom-tags, the entry for cast literal-key on (value) becomes tagged.
        Return tagged.
    Done.

    /// The value of a mark an axiom literal carries — `:ReleasedBy "closer"` — or "".
    Bind text to literal-mark, given (the node literal, the text mark):
        Define place as 4.
        While place is less than the number of literal's children, repeat:
            If (cast field-of on (literal, place))'s word is mark, return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (literal, place + 1)).
            Increment place by 2.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// `RequireCrossableResult`: a number, a fact, or a voidable text, number or address comes back.
    Bind void or failure to require-crossable-result, given (the node result, the text language, the number at-row):
        If result's kind is "NumberType" or result's kind is "FactType", return.
        If result's kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner-kind as (cast field-of on (result, 1))'s kind.
            If inner-kind is "TextType" or inner-kind is "NumberType" or inner-kind is "AddressType", return.
        Done.
        If result's kind is "TextType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a {language} axiom gives back a 'voidable text', never a plain 'text'",
                "C says nothing is there by handing back nothing — `getenv` on an unset name, `strerror` on a code it does not know",
                at-row, "declare it as giving back a text",
                "Write 'Define {language} voidable text <name> as [ ... ].'")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a {language} axiom cannot give back a {cast type-words on (result)} yet",
            "A number, a fact and a voidable text cross back; nothing else does",
            at-row, "declare it as giving back a {cast type-words on (result)}",
            "Give back a number, a fact or a voidable text, and do the rest inside the source.")).
    Done.

    /// `CheckAxiomParameters`: what an axiom takes can cross, is named once, and is used.
    Bind void or failure to check-axiom-parameters unto checker, given (the node statement, the node literal,
            the text language, the node result, the series of node parameters):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define define-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Define literal-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (literal, 2)).
        If cast is-nothing on (result) and the number of parameters is greater than 0:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "'{name}' says nothing about what it gives back, so it is source rather than something to run — and source takes no parameters",
                "A parameter's value comes from a call, and nothing calls this: it is pasted once, above every axiom that can then use what it declares",
                define-row, "give '{name}' parameters",
                "Drop the 'given' clause — or say what running it gives back, as in 'Define {language} number {name}, given (…), as [ … ].'")).
        Done.
        Define source as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (literal, 1)).
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in parameters, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)).
            Define taken-kind as taken's kind.
            If taken-kind is not "NumberType" and taken-kind is not "FactType" and taken-kind is not "TextType" and taken-kind is not "AddressType":
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a {cast type-words on (taken)} cannot be handed to {language} source yet",
                    "A number, a fact and a text cross the boundary; nothing else does",
                    literal-row, "declare '{parameter-name}' as a {cast type-words on (taken)}",
                    "Take a number, a fact or a text instead, and do the rest inside the source.")).
            Done.
            If (the entry for parameter-name in seen) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{parameter-name}' is declared twice in this axiom's parameters",
                    "Each `the <name>` in the source has to name exactly one of them",
                    literal-row, "declare '{parameter-name}' twice", "Give them different names.")).
            Done.
            In seen, the entry for parameter-name becomes true.
            If cast mentions-parameter on (source, parameter-name) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this {language} source never uses 'the {parameter-name}'",
                    "A parameter reaches the source by its article — `the text path` here, `the path` in the source",
                    literal-row, "declare '{parameter-name}' without using it",
                    "Write 'the {parameter-name}' where the value belongs, or drop it from 'given'.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast bind-mark on (statement, ":HasParameterClause") is "true" and the number of parameters is 0:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' declares an empty parameter list", "",
                define-row, "write 'given ()' with nothing in it",
                "Drop the 'given' clause — an axiom that takes nothing needs none.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `CheckReleaseClause`: what frees an axiom's result is an axiom taking one address, and the
    /// result is an address to free.
    Bind void or failure to check-release-clause unto checker, given (the node literal, the text released,
            the text language, the node result, the number at-row):
        If released is "", return.
        Define freeable as false.
        If cast is-nothing on (result) is false and result's kind is "VoidableType":
            The freeable becomes (cast field-of on (result, 1))'s kind is "AddressType".
        Done.
        If freeable is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{released}' is named to free what this axiom gives back, but it does not give back an address",
                "only an address needs freeing — a number, a fact and a text are copied across the boundary and belong to Cufet once they arrive",
                at-row, "say how to free something that is not an address",
                "Drop the clause, or declare this axiom 'voidable address'.")).
        Done.
        Define found as cast one's look-up on (released).
        Define release as cast unknown-type.
        If found is not void:
            If found's established-by's kind is "AxiomLiteral", the release becomes found's established-by.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (release):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{released}' is named to free this axiom's result, but it is not an axiom",
                "freeing happens in the other language, so the thing that does it has to be foreign source too",
                at-row, "free an address with something that is not foreign source",
                "Declare it, as in 'Define {language} number {released}, given (the address held), as [ … ].'")).
        Done.
        Define taking as cast axiom-parameters on (release).
        Define takes-one-address as false.
        If the number of taking is 1:
            The takes-one-address becomes (cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (item 1 of taking, 1)))'s kind is "AddressType".
        Done.
        If takes-one-address is false:
            Define takes as "nothing".
            If the number of taking is greater than 0, the takes becomes cast amount-of on (the number of taking, "value").
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{released}' has to take exactly one address to free one, and it takes {takes}", "",
                at-row, "free an address with an axiom that cannot be handed one",
                "Declare it 'given (the address held)'.")).
        Done.
        Cast note on (literal, ":ReleaseAxiom", release).
    Done.

    /// `AxiomBehind`: the literal a name stands for, following names bound to names — or none.
    Bind node to axiom-behind unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define reached as said.
        Define hops as 0.
        While hops is less than 64, repeat:
            If reached's kind is "AxiomLiteral", return reached.
            If reached's kind is not "VariableReference", return cast unknown-type.
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (reached, 1))).
            If found is void, return cast unknown-type.
            Define established as found's established-by.
            If established's kind is "AxiomLiteral", return established.
            If established's kind is not "VariableReference", return cast unknown-type.
            The reached becomes established.
            Increment hops by 1.
        Done.
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    /// The tag a declaration gave this literal, or none when nothing declared it.
    Bind node to axiom-tag-of unto checker, given (the node literal):
        Define tagged as the entry for cast literal-key on (literal) in one's axiom-tags.
        If tagged is void, return cast unknown-type.
        Return tagged.
    Done.

    /// A bare axiom literal's type — the one its declaration gave it.
    Bind node or failure to infer-axiom-literal unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define tagged as cast one's axiom-tag-of on (said).
        If cast is-none on (tagged) is false, return tagged.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this is foreign source, and nothing says what language it is in",
            "An axiom takes its language from the declaration it is the value of",
            cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)), "write foreign source outside a declaration that names its language",
            "Give it a name first: 'Define c-language <name> as [ ... ].'")).
    Done.

    /// `RunResultOf`: what running this axiom gives back, refusing one that never said.
    Bind node or failure to run-result-of, given (the node tagged, the number at-row):
        Define result as cast field-of on (tagged, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (result) is false, return result.
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tagged, 1)).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this {language} axiom does not say what it gives back",
            "Cufet cannot read a C listing to find out — an `int` might be a number, a fact, or a handle, and only the person who wrote the source knows which",
            at-row, "run foreign source that never declared a result",
            "Say so where it is declared: 'Define {language} number <name> as [ ... ].'")).
    Done.

    /// An axiom whose source is not known where it is being run.
    Bind text to source-not-reachable, given (the node axiom, the number at-row):
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (axiom, 1)).
        Return cast refusal-of on ("this {language} axiom cannot be run from here — its source is not known at this point",
            "an axiom is the foreign text itself, and running one pastes that text; a name bound to an axiom can be run, but one arriving through a parameter or handed back by a function has no text to paste",
            at-row, "run an axiom whose source is decided at run time",
            "Run it where it is declared, or bind the axiom to a name and run that name.").
    Done.

    /// `RunAxiomOnReturn`: returning a declared axiom runs it.
    Bind node or failure to run-axiom-on-return unto checker, given (the node returning, the node value, the number at-row):
        Define literal as cast one's axiom-behind on (value).
        Define tagged as cast one's axiom-tag-of on (literal).
        If cast is-none on (tagged):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("an axiom can only be run by returning one that was declared",
                "Foreign source runs from a name, so there is always a declaration to read the language and the source off",
                at-row, "run foreign source that has no declaration",
                "Declare it first: 'Define c-language <name> as [ ... ].' — then return that name.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's require-language-pulled on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tagged, 1)), at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Cast note on (returning, ":RunsAxiom", literal).
        Return cast run-result-of on (tagged, at-row) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// A cast that reaches an axiom — by name, with its source in hand, or as a value with only its
    /// written type. Gives back what running it gives, or none when the callee is no axiom.
    Bind node or failure to check-axiom-call unto checker, given (the node call, the node callee, the node call-args,
            the number at-row, the fact as-value, the fact passes-off):
        If callee's kind is not "VariableReference", return cast unknown-type.
        Define callee-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
        Define found as cast one's look-up on (callee-name).
        If found is void, return cast unknown-type.
        Define axiom as found's shape.
        If axiom's kind is not "AxiomType", return cast unknown-type.
        Define literal as cast one's axiom-behind on (callee).
        Define tagged as cast unknown-type.
        If cast is-none on (literal) is false, the tagged becomes cast one's axiom-tag-of on (literal).
        If cast is-none on (tagged) is false:
            If as-value is false and passes-off:
                Cast one's check-pass-off on (cast unknown-type, "'{callee-name}'", at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tagged, 1)).
            Cast one's require-language-pulled on (language, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's check-foreign-arguments on (call-args, cast axiom-parameters on (literal), language, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Define ran as cast run-result-of on (tagged, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Cast note on (call, ":RunsAxiom", literal).
            Return ran.
        Done.
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (axiom, 2)):
            Return a failure (cast source-not-reachable on (axiom, at-row)).
        Done.
        If as-value is false and passes-off:
            Cast one's check-pass-off on (cast unknown-type, "'{callee-name}'", at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-axiom-value-call on (call-args, axiom, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Cast note on (call, ":RunsAxiomValue", cast flag on (true)).
        Return cast field-of on (axiom, 2).
    Done.

    /// `CheckForeignArguments`: a call matches what the axiom's declaration takes.
    Bind void or failure to check-foreign-arguments unto checker, given (the node call-args, the series of node parameters,
            the text language, the number at-row):
        Define given-args as call-args's children.
        If the number of given-args is not the number of parameters:
            Define was as "were".
            If the number of given-args is 1, the was becomes "was".
            Define parameter-spellings as a series of text.
            For each pair in parameters, repeat:
                Insert "the {cast type-words on (cast field-of on (pair, 1))} {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 2))}" into parameter-spellings.
            Done.
            Define listing as "".
            For each piece in parameter-spellings, repeat:
                If listing is not "", the listing becomes listing joined to ", ".
                The listing becomes listing joined to piece.
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "this {language} source takes {cast amount-of on (the number of parameters, "value")}, and {the number of given-args} {was} given", "",
                at-row, "pass {cast amount-of on (the number of given-args, "value")}",
                "It is declared 'given ({listing})'.")).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in given-args, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define pair as item place of parameters.
            Define wanted as cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)).
            Define actual as cast one's infer on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (actual) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, actual) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "'{parameter-name}' takes a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, but a {cast type-words on (actual)} was given", "",
                    at-row, "pass a {cast type-words on (actual)} for '{parameter-name}'",
                    "Give it a {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `CheckAxiomValueCall`: a call matches a WRITTEN axiom type, by position.
    Bind void or failure to check-axiom-value-call unto checker, given (the node call-args, the node axiom, the number at-row):
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (axiom, 1)).
        Cast one's require-language-pulled on (language, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define given-args as call-args's children.
        Define wanted-types as (cast field-of on (axiom, 3))'s children.
        If the number of given-args is not the number of wanted-types:
            Define was as "were".
            If the number of given-args is 1, the was becomes "was".
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "this {language} axiom takes {cast amount-of on (the number of wanted-types, "value")}, and {the number of given-args} {was} given", "",
                at-row, "pass {cast amount-of on (the number of given-args, "value")}",
                "It is written '{cast type-words on (axiom)}'.")).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in given-args, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define wanted as item place of wanted-types.
            Define actual as cast one's infer on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (actual) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, actual) is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                    "value {place} of this {language} axiom takes a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, but a {cast type-words on (actual)} was given", "",
                    at-row, "pass a {cast type-words on (actual)} there", "Give it a {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// An axiom that never said what it gives back, reached for as a value.
    Bind text to axiom-used-as-value, given (the text name, the node axiom, the number at-row):
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (axiom, 1)).
        Return cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is {language} source, and can only be run by returning it",
            "Foreign source is not a value that can be printed, stored, or passed",
            at-row, "use '{name}' as a value",
            "Wrap it: 'Bind number to <name>, {name}.' — then use that function.").
    Done.

    /// `the text at <address>` — read through a foreign pointer; void reads as void.
    Bind node or failure to infer-text-at unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define held as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (held):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the text at' reads through a foreign address, and nothing here says what this is",
                "only an address from foreign source can be read through, and this name does not resolve to a value at all",
                at-row, "read text at something with no type",
                "Give it an address from foreign source — the result of an axiom declared 'voidable address'.")).
        Done.
        Define readable as held's kind is "AddressType".
        If held's kind is "VoidableType", the readable becomes (cast field-of on (held, 1))'s kind is "AddressType".
        If readable is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the text at' reads through a foreign address, and this is a {cast type-words on (held)}",
                "the only thing an address can be read through is this phrase, and the only thing this phrase reads is an address",
                at-row, "read text at a {cast type-words on (held)}", "Give it an address from foreign source.")).
        Done.
        Return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
    Done.

    /// `RequireRabbitForAddress`: a foreign pointer may only be held inside a rabbit.
    Bind void or failure to require-rabbit-for-address unto checker, given (the node shape, the text name, the number at-row):
        If one's rabbit-depth is greater than 0, return.
        Define holds as shape's kind is "AddressType".
        If shape's kind is "VoidableType", the holds becomes (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s kind is "AddressType".
        If holds is false, return.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' holds a foreign address, and one can only be held inside a rabbit",
            "a rabbit block is where region-scoped memory work happens, so it is also where a pointer's lifetime is answered for — the rabbit that knows when the region dies is what knows when the pointer dies",
            at-row, "hold a foreign address outside a rabbit", "Wrap the work in 'Pull a rabbit. ... Done.'")).
    Done.

    /// An axiom written as a type that never says what it gives back — `ResolveParamType`'s refusal.
    Bind void or failure to check-written-axiom, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is not "AxiomType" or cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (shape, 2)) is false, return.
        Define language as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
        Return a failure "error\tThat doesn't work: a {language} axiom written as a type has to say what it gives back. 'the c-language axiom job' cannot be a parameter, a field, or an element type, because nothing could be done with what running it produces. Say the result: 'the {language} number axiom job'.".
    Done.
Done.
